From: mscharged-port
Subject: Give the host overlay a texture pack's replacement of a game texture
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host presentation (host menus, texture packs). Apply after 0121.

Recharged's menus draw some of the game's own pictures themselves (the
players' hands and their numbers, the pause menu's header): they read the
game's texture and make an ImGui texture of it. With an HD texture pack the
game's own draws of those textures show the pack's images, the menus still
showed the original ones.

aurora_imgui_texture_replacement(tex_obj, tlut_obj, &width, &height) looks a
game texture up as the game's draws do (by its data pointer, else by its
hash and its palette's) and hands the replacement it finds to ImGui: a view
of the replacement's own texture (any format the pack has, PNG or DDS), kept
with that texture until shutdown, the same one each time. A streamed
replacement may first be its thumbnail, so the host asks again while it
shows. 0 without a replacement, and with the SDL renderer (no GPU device).

diff --git a/include/aurora/imgui.h b/include/aurora/imgui.h
index 626d8c1..4c38e74 100644
--- a/include/aurora/imgui.h
